+ side_effects:
+   - Installs a user-level background daemon (launchd on macOS, systemd user timer on Linux) via install_daemon.sh. Runs every 15 min. Does NOT run as root.
+   - Writes local files under ~/.openclaw/workspace/skills/proactive-agent/ (token.json, config.json, memory.db, daemon.log). No files written outside this directory.
+   - Creates and edits events in your Google/Nextcloud calendar (OpenClaw calendar only by default).
+   - Makes outbound HTTPS requests to Google Calendar API, and optionally Notion API, Telegram API, GitHub API, clawhub.ai — only when the corresponding feature is enabled in config.json.
+   - All features can be individually disabled via feature_* flags in config.json before running the daemon.
+ ## Security & Privacy
+ | What | Detail |
+ |------|--------|
+ | **Credentials stay local** | `credentials.json`, `token.json`, `config.json` are stored only in `~/.openclaw/workspace/skills/proactive-agent/`. Never uploaded anywhere. |
+ | **Background daemon** | `install_daemon.sh` installs a user-level timer (launchd/systemd). Runs as your user only — never root. Uninstall anytime: `launchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/ai.openclaw.proactive-claw.plist` |
+ | **Calendar writes** | Only writes to the `OpenClaw` calendar it creates. Never modifies your existing calendars unless you explicitly confirm. |
+ | **Network calls** | Only to: Google Calendar API, and optionally Notion, Telegram, GitHub, clawhub.ai — each gated by a `feature_*` flag in `config.json`. |
+ | **Nextcloud password** | Use an app-specific password, not your account password. Generate at `your-nextcloud/settings/personal/security`. |
+ | **Safe by default** | All optional integrations (`feature_voice`, `feature_team_awareness`, `feature_cross_skill`, etc.) are `false` by default. Enable only what you need. |
+ | **Inspect before running** | Review `setup.sh` and `install_daemon.sh` before executing. Both are plain shell scripts with no obfuscated downloads. |